# dotenvx + Bitwarden (local env)

Canonical how-to: [`docs/dotenvx.md`](docs/dotenvx.md). Stack: [dotenvx](https://dotenvx.com/) · [Bitwarden custody](https://dotenvx.com/docs/custody/bitwarden/).

## Model

| Place | Format | Private key |
|---|---|---|
| Git (this public repo) | **Encrypted** `.env` (`encrypted:…`) | Never |
| Dev PC (Win/macOS) | Same encrypted `.env` from git | Bitwarden (`dotenvx bitwarden up`) / local `.env.keys` |
| VPS `/opt/twitch-telegram-bot` | **Plaintext** `.env` (compose / deploy) | N/A |

Sync between devices = `git pull` of ciphertext + Bitwarden for the private key. No Resilio / Dropbox / side copies of `.env`.

**Trade-off:** anyone with the Bitwarden private key can decrypt every historical commit that contains that ciphertext. Protect the vault item; rotate the keypair after any leak.

## Agent must

- Load via `dotenv_loader` / `config.py` — never invent a second parser
- Prefer `dotenvx set KEY "value"` for encrypted updates, then **commit** the encrypted `.env` (and push when syncing devices)
- After changes to critical keys, also sync VPS **plaintext** per [`twitch-client-secret.mdc`](twitch-client-secret.mdc)
- Run local bot with `dotenvx run -- python main.py` (or Bitwarden unlock / `.env.keys`)
- Keep `.env.keys`, plaintext secrets, Hostkey/API keys, `BW_SESSION` out of chat, commits, logs — print counts/prefixes only
- Refuse committing `.env.keys` or plaintext secrets; remind `dotenvx bitwarden up` if a private key appears on disk after encrypt/rotate
- Know that `dotenvx bitwarden pull` needs a **local custody reference** from a prior `bitwarden up` on this machine; otherwise materialize `.env.keys` via `bw get password <item-id>` (never print the key)
- Docker image: no `.env` / `.env.keys` (`.dockerignore`); VPS deploy must keep restoring plaintext `.env` (not the git ciphertext)

## Agent must not

- Use Resilio / Dropbox / USB as the env sync path
- Put private key or vault session in source / README / rules examples with real values
- Commit `.env.keys` or a plaintext `.env`
- Replace VPS plaintext workflow with encrypted-only without an explicit user request
- Log decrypted env or `bw` / Hostkey tokens
- Assume Bitwarden custody is done while `.env.keys` still holds `DOTENV_PRIVATE_KEY=…`

## Quick commands

```bash
dotenvx set SOME_KEY "new-value"
git add .env
git commit -m "encrypt .env"

export BW_SESSION="$(bw unlock --raw)"
dotenvx bitwarden up        # after first encrypt / rotate
dotenvx run -- python main.py
```

PowerShell may block `.ps1` — use the commands above or `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts\env-run.ps1`.
